shop without purpose. **N: f3-d2** is passive.  \n\n---\n\n**Best choice**: Castle to safety and unpin the d4 pawn.  \n\n**Evaluation**: Castling (K: e1-g1) is the most improving move, safeguarding the king, connecting rooks, and resolving the pin on d4.  \n\n**Reason**: King safety is top priority; the pinned pawn limits our options, castling breaks the pin instantly and develops rook. Alternatives like Nf3-e5 allow Qe4+ checks or queen retreat to safety without major gain.  \n\n**Answer**: K: e1-g1"}
